! Source for BuildingSurface:Detailed (all 60 objects of this class): geometry and materials: the polygons give the areas listed per zone in the xlsx raw_data (see the Zone comments); layer data are not in the documents unless a Source comment says so. Kept: prototype values.
! Vertex formulas of the BuildingSurface:Detailed objects: the coordinates are relative to the origin of the zone of the surface (the Zone objects give the origins), X to the east, Y to the north, Z up. Every coordinate is a length in feet x 0.3048 m/ft; coordinates that are not a whole number of feet are written as feet with 4 decimals and marked (position). NREL PDF Table 13 (Strip Mall: 22,500 ft2, 1 floor, aspect ratio 4.0, floor-to-floor height 17 ft) gives a floor plate of 22,500 / 1 = 22,500 ft2 and W = sqrt(plate x aspect ratio) = 300.0 ft, D = W / aspect ratio = 75.0 ft; for comparison the exterior walls of the IDF span X = 0.00 to 300.00 ft, Y = 0.00 to 75.00 ft, Z = 0.00 to 16.99 ft (zone origin + coordinate). The prototype generator and the origin offsets are not in the documents.
